Now we need to find out how long it takes for them to complete a combined total of 360 pieces. We can simply divide the total number of pieces by the combined rate of work to find the time it takes in minutes:

Time (minutes) = Total pieces / Combined rate = 360 / 6 = \boxed{\textbf{60 minutes}}

Finally, to find out the hours it takes, we simply divide the number of minutes by 60:

Hours = Minutes / 60 = 60 / 60 = \boxed{\textbf{1}}

So, it will take Kalinda and her mom \boxed{\textbf{1 hour}} to complete the puzzle.

